# THE DATA LEMMA, OUT OF PROFILE (SPEC.md §5.2; issue #133): the string half
# covers only xsd:string and rdf:langString literals on named individuals. Here
# :v is asserted "1"^^xsd:integer with range xsd:integer, a typed literal that is
# neither a string nor a date-time, so :v is NOT literal-asserted. Its assertion and range stay out
# of profile as omissions, and the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2). The
# disjointness and the typing of :j are still read.

@prefix :     <https://example.org/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:A owl:disjointWith :B .
:v a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:integer .
:j a :D ; :v "1"^^xsd:integer .
